  "dispositions": {
    "accepted": [
      "The controlled missing-instanceId versus instanceId=1 transition is reproduced for DayZDiag 1.29.0.163709.",
      "The successful run reached modded MissionServer.OnInit with server and multiplayer true and retained a PID-owned game endpoint through the bound.",
      "The query socket bound 0.0.0.0, so the entire process was not loopback-only.",
      "In the retained direct RestartMission run, the tested Mission static reinitialized and the tested World static persisted in one PID.",
      "The lifecycle run exited with 0xC0000005 and did not demonstrate clean restart operation."
    ],
    "rejected": [
      "The whole successful process was loopback-only.",
      "The lifecycle probe is a safe reusable restart implementation.",
      "Direct GetGame().RestartMission() is equivalent to authenticated admin #restart.",
      "The truncated landscape warning or CE restoration is the proven crash cause.",
      "These diagnostic probes certify public or production servers."
    ],
    "unresolved": [
      "Why the failed log does not print the executable's missing-instanceId diagnostic.",
      "The native cause of 0xC0000005.",
      "Stable post-restart operation and clean exit.",
      "Authenticated #restart lifecycle semantics.",
      "Static behavior beyond the two tested fields, modules, and build.",
      "Fresh full-body official Server Configuration page review because the direct request returned HTTP 403."
    ]
  },
  "proposedEnglish": [
    {
      "path": "en/09-server-admin/03-server-cfg.md",
      "action": "replace instanceId table row",
      "text": "| `instanceId` | int | required in the tested build; no default established | Identifies the server instance and selects persistence under `storage_<instanceId>/`. In a controlled DayZDiag `1.29.0.163709` startup, omitting this key terminated before the Mission module loaded; adding only `instanceId = 1;` let `MissionServer.OnInit()` run and selected `storage_1`. Set an explicit, unique 32-bit integer for each instance. This scoped diagnostic result is not production-server certification. |"
    },
    {
      "path": "en/09-server-admin/01-server-setup.md",
      "action": "add after sample serverDZ.cfg block",
      "text": "Keep `instanceId` explicit. In a controlled DayZDiag `1.29.0.163709` test, a config without it terminated before the Mission module loaded, while the otherwise identical config with `instanceId = 1;` reached `MissionServer.OnInit()`. This verifies the diagnostic startup path only; it does not certify `DayZServer_x64.exe`, client connectivity, or public production hosting."
    },
    {
      "path": "en/09-server-admin/01-server-setup.md",
      "action": "add to local-server verification discussion",
      "text": "A loopback game bind does not prove that every socket in the process is loopback-only. In the same diagnostic run, the game endpoint was `127.0.0.1:<game-port>` but the configured Steam query endpoint was `0.0.0.0:<steamQueryPort>`. Check each PID-owned endpoint and your firewall separately; a wildcard bind alone does not prove public reachability."
    },
    {
      "path": "en/01-enforce-script/08-memory-management.md",
      "action": "replace first paragraph under Static State and Mission Lifecycle",
      "text": "A controlled DayZDiag `1.29.0.163709` dedicated-server probe called `GetGame().RestartMission()` once from a `MissionServer` callback. In the same PID, the Mission script module and mission `init.c` loaded again: a Mission-module `static int` initializer ran again (`100` to `101` in each `OnInit()`), while a World-module `static int` was not reinitialized and advanced from `201` to `202`. The process then exited with `0xC0000005` before its clean-exit marker, so treat this as a bounded module-lifetime observation—not a safe restart recipe or evidence about authenticated `#restart`, reconnects, or process restarts."
    }
  ],
